UPDATE pbh_books SET title='Harbinger: The Prophet''s Game', author='Steven Harrison', genres='["Mystery & Thriller"]', image='/images/latest/harbinger-prophets-game.webp', amazon='https://www.amazon.co.uk/dp/B0HFN1RQ7G', feature='/books/harbinger-the-prophets-game.html', photo='/images/featured-authors/steven-harrison.webp', tag='Crime Thriller', hook='A killer leaves a black feather beside each victim, drawing Detective Sam Rourke into a network of corruption that protects Chicago’s elite.', description='Three victims. Three methods. One black feather.

Chicago’s wealthiest citizens are being murdered and displayed for the city to see. Beside each victim is a black feather. The press calls the killer the Harbinger, a self-appointed judge targeting people whose money and influence have kept them beyond consequence.

Detective Sam Rourke has no interest in the mythology. Military-trained and carrying the weight of an old war, a fading faith and a father disappearing into dementia, Rourke believes the evidence will tell him what happened if he’s patient enough to follow it.

When the killer contacts disgraced investigative reporter Miles Carter, Miles sees a chance to reclaim the career he lost. Rourke sees someone trying to get ahead of the investigation by deciding which version of the story the public hears first.

With each murder, the evidence leads deeper into powerful law firms, fraudulent property developments and Chicago politics. The victims begin to look like pieces of something built to stay buried. And the closer Rourke comes to understanding why they were chosen, the harder it becomes to separate justice from vengeance.

Harbinger: The Prophet’s Game is the first book in the Sam Rourke Thriller Series.', status='archive', sort_index='0' WHERE lower(title)=lower('Harbinger: The Prophet''s Game');
